Watermelon-1 Privacy Policy

Effective date: October 6, 2026

Operator: xu ning

Watermelon-1 (the “App”) is a music app for playing, sequencing, recording, and exporting rhythms on iPhone and iPad. This policy also applies to the Watermelon-1 Instrument and Watermelon-1 Drum Machine AUv3 plug-ins included with the App. The information below describes the current version of these products.

1. Data processed in the App

The App processes the positions of your touches while playing, sequencer steps and parameters, selected sounds, MIDI input, and the resulting audio on your device. The recording feature captures audio generated by the App. It does not record audio from your device’s microphone.

The App uses local storage on your device to save sequencer patterns, sounds, and settings. Recordings are stored as audio files in the App’s local folder. Each new recording also includes a snapshot of the sequencer pattern and sound settings at the end of the recording. The export feature generates audio or MIDI files on your device. Bluetooth MIDI pairing is handled by an iOS system interface. Connected USB and Bluetooth MIDI devices can send performance commands to the App.

2. Data collection and use

The current version has no accounts, advertisements, third-party analytics, or tracking features. It does not upload your performances, recordings, MIDI data, or usage data to a developer-operated server. Local data is used to play sounds, save settings, record, play back, and export. We do not sell this data or use it to track you across apps.

If you choose to contact us by email, we will receive the email address and content you provide. We use this information only to reply to you and handle your request. Please do not include unnecessary sensitive information in support emails.

3. Sharing, host apps, and system services

A selected recording or exported file is transferred to a destination you choose only when you use the system share sheet or import the file into another app. The destination app or service processes that file under its own privacy policy. iOS system services, such as device backups, may also process locally stored data according to your system settings.

The AUv3 plug-ins process audio and MIDI in compatible host apps. A host app may save plug-in state in its project file. Saving, syncing, and sharing that project are controlled by the host app.

4. Retention and deletion

Patterns and settings remain on your device until you change them or delete the App and its data. Recordings and their associated settings snapshots remain on your device until you delete the corresponding recording from Recording History or delete the App and its data. Temporary files created for export may be cleared by the system. Copies that you have shared, copied to other apps, or included in a device backup must be managed or deleted separately in those locations.

Support emails are retained for the time needed to handle the conversation and reasonable follow-up. You may request deletion of information related to that correspondence using the email address below, except where retention is required by law.

5. Your choices

You can change patterns and settings, delete recordings, and choose whether to connect MIDI devices or export or share files. You can also manage Bluetooth permissions and device backups in iOS Settings. For support emails you send voluntarily, you can request access, correction, or deletion using the contact information below.

6. Changes to this policy

If the App’s data practices change, we will update this policy and its effective date and update the App Store privacy disclosures as applicable.
